# If you prefer the allow list template instead of the deny list, see community template:
# https://github.com/github/gitignore/blob/main/community/Golang/Go.AllowList.gitignore
#
# Binaries for programs and plugins
*.exe
*.exe~
*.dll
*.so
*.dylib

# Test binary, built with `go test -c`
*.test

# Code coverage profiles and other test artifacts
*.out
coverage.*
*.coverprofile
profile.cov

# Dependency directories (remove the comment below to include it)
# vendor/

# Go workspace file
go.work
go.work.sum

# env file
.env

# Editor/IDE
.idea/
.vscode/

# Build output
/bin/
# A bare `go build ./cmd/...` writes the binary here rather than into bin/.
/valmind

# Node dependencies and build output, anywhere in the tree. web/.gitignore already covers
# the SPA's own; this catches a second package appearing elsewhere. The one exception is
# web/build/, which stays in the tree without its contents because web/embed.go embeds it
# (ADR-092) — web/build/.gitignore is what keeps that arrangement.
node_modules/
.svelte-kit/

# Agent tooling and the design pack: kept local, not tracked
.claude/
CLAUDE.md
AGENTS.md
/docs/*
!/docs/README.md
!/docs/installation.md
!/docs/usage.md
!/docs/configuration.md
!/docs/operations.md
!/docs/troubleshooting.md
!/docs/development.md
!/docs/api.md
!/docs/architecture.md

# Lint tooling output, written into the working tree by a `make lint` run.
/jscpd-report/
/semgrep.lint

# Thunderstore packages are downloaded, never committed (ADR-108).
# A local corpus lives here and is reached by VALMIN_MOD_CORPUS.
/mods/

# Release artefacts, written by `make release-snapshot` (goreleaser --clean owns it).
/dist/
# The dependency inventory that goes into the release archive (`make inventory`).
/inventory/
# The integration images, exported by `make save-images` to be carried to another machine.
/images.tar
